{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1, node2, and node3 as a healthy three-member MariaDB Galera cluster.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three nodes ultimately report MariaDB active and enabled, cluster size 3, Primary status, Connected, Synced, Ready, and the expected cluster and node identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-20f78eb72e2b4b90","cmd-269e120a6f72445c","cmd-44ab339072a2491f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Writes accepted through any member must be available from the other members.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Writes were issued independently through node1, node2, and node3. Final queries on every member returned the same seven rows, including each member's post-restart write.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab020defb10d46ab","cmd-38074f21610b4e8e","cmd-ffeced652e634645","cmd-20f78eb72e2b4b90","cmd-269e120a6f72445c","cmd-44ab339072a2491f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the database available when one cluster member is unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After node3 was stopped and confirmed inactive, node2 accepted a new write while the remaining cluster reported size 2, Primary, Synced, and Ready; node1 concurrently remained healthy and contained that write.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7edea4057a494ac4","cmd-14ba0d9379644fd4","cmd-9dc583f883c74e0f"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Automatically resynchronize an unavailable member when it returns.","status":"satisfied","summary":"When node3 was restarted, it automatically became active, Synced, Ready, and part of a three-member Primary component, and contained the row committed during its absence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81c352c71b2c409e"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, cluster configuration, boot enablement, bootstrap/join operations, the bounded node3 disruption, evidence-table writes, and required node restarts all had direct roles in implementation or verification. The initially literal wsrep_node_address values were immediately corrected as part of completing the configuration, rather than being an unrelated experiment. Temporary installer/configuration artifacts were absent after the verified reboots; all nodes had healthy package state and no failed services. The new MariaDB listeners are expected task-related state. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete for every node: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart scheduling, changed boot identity, and recovered service, cluster, and data state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate all three changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d6d44766fea4df6","cmd-b46c4859c6df4a57","cmd-2eee9f0973ba419a","cmd-101916a061de4307","cmd-bc0fd014c905489e","cmd-538ed78691d5447b","cmd-ee9f3ca30fcc423b","cmd-ef86aad9003640f8","cmd-519b9051e04544f2","cmd-a19cfac0aa7c4a98","cmd-213c1d478a7e4f93","cmd-b70341570a574249","cmd-991de725b84a4090","cmd-73374864c02e472a","cmd-bae12ddce95b4638","cmd-703837ea653d4bab","cmd-ddf706ee840d45d3","cmd-740813197d754cd4","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence: a healthy three-member Galera cluster, writes through every member replicated everywhere, continued writable quorum during a bounded single-member outage, automatic synchronization on return, and successful persistence and recovery across required restarts of all managed nodes.","limitations":[]}
